@startuml
title How a fresh installation reaches calibrated, running feeds

|bootstrap setup|
start
:Create the administrator and sign in;
:Accept the public sources' terms;
:Start provisioning;

|Provisioning, system run|
:system_provision\npublish system_core: feeds, authored calibrations,\nadapter catalogue;
note right
  Feeds of a class that is not
  released do not announce,
  so no demand starts them.
end note
fork
  :start_calibration\nstart synthetic_calibration_workflow;
  |synthetic_calibration_workflow|
  :load_public_rates\nofficial service backfills each accepted source;
  :calibrate_feeds\napplied run: levels, spreads,\nvariance inputs and fits;
  :approve_within_policy\nfits that pass the policy's rules\nare approved by the policy;
  :tell_reviewer\ninbox names the exceptions;
  |Provisioning, system run|
  if (profile orders the release?) then (Acme, demo)
    :release_feeds\nthe feeds start from calibrated levels;
  else (production)
    :an operator presses Start feeds;
  endif
fork again
  :start_tenant_setup;
  |Tenant run|
  :publish bundles, parties, staff,\nphotos, subscriptions, trades;
  :complete_provisioning;
end fork

|Each business day|
:scheduler starts synthetic_calibration_workflow;
note right
  Exceptions wait in the reviewer's
  inbox; a person approves or rejects
  them through the same review verb.
  A feed takes a new calibration
  at its next start.
end note
stop
@enduml
